# PROPOSED, NOT APPLIED -- contracts are signed by a person, not by a tool.
#
# What this changes, and why:
#
#   1. gpio_spi_fallback_result.verdict  PASS -> WARNING_evidence_gap
#      The run it cites, 20260820T063111Z_gate10_gpio0_3_clocked_return, is not
#      on disk. `py -3 -m QKD_PROJ.orchestrator.evidence
#      QKD_PROJ/docs/evidence/gate10-conditions.json` reduces this gate to
#      outcome=primary_run_missing.
#
#   2. observed_rx -> observed_rx_unverifiable, kept verbatim.
#      Deleting the number would lose what was seen. Leaving it under its old
#      key would let it keep reading as a measurement.
#
#   3. A corroboration block, with closes_gate: false.
#      Gate 11's SRAM run holds a JTAG scan and a program, and no GPIO readback
#      at all -- so citing it instead would move the gap rather than fill it.
#      The scope capture isolates the McSPI fault on its own, without any GPIO
#      read, and is the strongest thing that survives here. It wrote no
#      RunRecord.
#
#   4. reinstatement_requires: an approved re-run, a RunRecord holding the
#      received frame, and a reduction that reports satisfied. No hardware was
#      run to produce this patch.
#
# The contract status line changes with it, because the current one asserts
# `gpio_spi_fallback_verified` and that is the claim under question.
#
# To apply, after review:   git apply QKD_PROJ/contracts/proposals/2026-08-21-gate10-evidence-gap.patch
# To see it first:          git apply --check --stat <the same path>
#
diff --git a/QKD_PROJ/contracts/gate10-spi-clocked-return.yaml b/QKD_PROJ/contracts/gate10-spi-clocked-return.yaml
index 0c0af22..db327af 100644
